TokenId Token ID to escrow atomically during creation.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:22:        address prizeToken;\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:23:        uint256 prizeTokenId;\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:30:    /// @notice Emitted after a raffle clone is initialized, registered, funded, and active.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:31:    /// @param raffleId One-based canonical raffle identifier.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:32:    /// @param raffle Newly created fixed-target ERC-1167 clone.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:33:    /// @param sponsor Prize depositor and pre-end empty-raffle refund authority.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:34:    /// @param sponsorRecipient Immutable recipient of sponsor quote proceeds and any returned prize.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:35:    /// @param prizeToken ERC-721 contract of the escrowed prize.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:36:    /// @param prizeTokenId Token ID of the escrowed prize.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:37:    /// @param quoteToken Immutable canonical six-decimal USDC contract used by the raffle.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:42:        uint256 indexed raffleId,\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:43:        address indexed raffle,\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:46:        address prizeToken,\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:47:        uint256 prizeTokenId,\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:72:    /// @notice Raised when the prize contract does not report ERC-721 interface support.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:73:    /// @param prizeToken Rejected prize-token contract.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:74:    error UnsupportedPrizeToken(address prizeToken);\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:76:    /// @notice Raised when a raffle is configured with a zero reserve entry threshold.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:93:    /// @notice Raised when the exact configured prize is not owned by an active clone after escrow.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:94:    /// @param raffle Newly created clone expected to hold the prize and report `Active`.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:95:    /// @param prizeToken ERC-721 prize contract.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:96:    /// @param prizeTokenId Configured prize token ID.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:97:    error PrizeEscrowVerificationFailed(address raffle, address prizeToken, uint256 prizeTokenId);\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:101:    /// @notice Creates, initializes, registers, and funds one autonomous fixed-target raffle clone atomically.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:102:    /// @param params Sponsor-selected recipient, prize, reserve, and timing configuration.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:103:    /// @return raffle Address of the newly created and activated clone.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:104:    function createRaffle(CreateRaffleParams calldata params) external returns (address raffle);\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:108:    /// @notice Returns the immutable canonical six-decimal USDC contract used by every raffle.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:109:    /// @return quoteTokenAddress Canonical USDC contract address trusted by this deployment.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:112:    /// @notice Returns the immutable Chainlink VRF v2.5 native direct-funding wrapper used by every raffle.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:116:    /// @notice Returns the immutable recipient of protocol fees from every raffle.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:120:    /// @notice Returns the fixed Chainlink callback execution limit used by every raffle.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:124:    /// @notice Returns the fixed Chainlink confirmation count used by every raffle.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:129:    /// @return implementation Locked raffle implementation address.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:130:    function raffleImplementation() external view returns (address implementation);\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:132:    /// @notice Returns the lifetime number of successfully created raffles.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:133:    /// @return count Latest one-based raffle identifier and total registered raffle count.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:134:    function raffleCount() external view returns (uint256 count);\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:136:    /// @notice Returns whether an address is a raffle registered by this factory.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:137:    /// @param raffle Address to check.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:139:    function isRaffle(address raffle) external view returns (bool registered);\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:141:    /// @notice Returns the canonical raffle address for an identifier.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:142:    /// @param raffleId One-based raffle identifier.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:143:    /// @return raffle Registered clone address, or the zero address for an unknown identifier.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:144:    function raffleById(uint256 raffleId) external view returns (address raffle);\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:146:    /// @notice Returns the canonical identifier assigned to a raffle address.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:147:    /// @param raffle Address to query.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:148:    /// @return raffleId One-based identifier, or zero for an unregistered address.\n./packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:149:    function idByRaffle(address raffle) external view returns (uint256 raffleId);\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:19:/// @title raffle.fun Raffle Escrow and Entry Ticket\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:21:/// @notice Escrows one NFT and sells fixed-price USDC entries through one transferable ERC-721 ticket per purchase.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:24:///      owners burn them for redemption or refund. Each raffle is a fixed, non-upgradeable ERC-1167 clone with no\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:26:///      atomically burns the ticket while receiving the NFT or cash prize.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:33:    /// @notice Inclusive global entry-number range represented by one sequential ERC-721 ticket.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:70:    IERC721 public override prizeToken;\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:73:    uint256 public override prizeTokenId;\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:76:    uint256 public override raffleId;\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:133:    bool public override prizeClaimed;\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:151:    /// @notice Deploys and locks the implementation shared by one factory's minimal-proxy raffles.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:183:                || params.protocolTreasury == address(0) || params.prizeToken == address(0)\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:187:        if (_isProtocolDestination(params.sponsor, params.prizeToken)) {\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:190:        if (_isProtocolDestination(params.protocolTreasury, params.prizeToken)) {\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:193:        if (_isProtocolDestination(params.sponsorRecipient, params.prizeToken)) {\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:200:        prizeToken = IERC721(params.prizeToken);\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:201:        prizeTokenId = params.prizeTokenId;\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:202:        raffleId = params.raffleId;\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:330:            if (prizeClaimed) revert PrizeAlreadyClaimed();\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:331:            prizeClaimed = true;\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:332:            deliveredPrizeToken = address(prizeToken);\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:333:            deliveredPrizeTokenId = prizeTokenId;\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:334:            prizeToken.transferFrom(address(this), winner, deliveredPrizeTokenId);\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:335:            if (prizeToken.ownerOf(deliveredPrizeTokenId) != winner) {\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:400:        if (prizeClaimed) revert PrizeAlreadyClaimed();\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:403:        prizeClaimed = true;\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:404:        prizeToken.transferFrom(address(this), recipient, prizeTokenId);\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:405:        if (prizeToken.ownerOf(prizeTokenId) != recipient) revert PrizeDeliveryVerificationFailed(recipient);\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:406:        emit SponsorPrizeReleased(msg.sender, recipient, address(prizeToken), prizeTokenId);\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:409:    /// @notice Accepts only the exact configured prize deposited by the factory for the sponsor.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:412:    /// @param operator ERC-721 transfer operator, which must be the canonical factory.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:414:    /// @param tokenId Transferred token ID, which must match the configured prize.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:415:    /// @return selector ERC-721 receiver acceptance selector.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:422:            status != Status.AwaitingPrize || msg.sender != address(prizeToken) || tokenId != prizeTokenId\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:477:    /// @notice Returns the fixed display name shared by every raffle ticket collection.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:478:    /// @return Exact ERC-721 collection name, `raffle.fun Ticket`.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:480:        return \"raffle.fun Ticket\";\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:483:    /// @notice Returns the fixed display symbol shared by every raffle ticket collection.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:484:    /// @return Exact ERC-721 collection symbol, `RAFFLE`.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:495:    /// @param auth Caller whose owner or operator authority is checked by ERC-721.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:498:        if (to != address(0) && _isProtocolDestination(to, address(prizeToken))) {\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:561:    ///      canonical USDC trust model assumes standard, non-rebasing, fee-free transfer semantics.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:565:        if (_isProtocolDestination(to, address(prizeToken))) revert InvalidQuoteDestination(to);\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:571:    /// @dev Reverts unless the raffle is in the expected lifecycle state.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:588:    ///      Initialization supplies the prospective prize token because clone storage is not populated yet; runtime\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:589:    ///      checks pass the stored prize token. Code-less addresses are not queried in the registry.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:591:    /// @param prizeToken_ Configured or prospective prize-token address to reject.\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:593:    function _isProtocolDestination(address destination, address prizeToken_)\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:600:            || destination == address(i_vrfV2PlusWrapper) || destination == prizeToken_\n./packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:601:            || destination == canonicalFactory.raffleImplementation();\n./DESIGN.md:2:Ethereum NFT raffle; immutable factory, ERC-1167 clones with immutable implementation. One entry costs 1,000,000 units of canonical six-decimal USDC. One purchase mints a transferable ERC721 ticket representing a contiguous inclusive range. Exactly one ERC721 prize is escrowed atomically at creation. Reserve met awards NFT and 95% sponsor / 5% treasury. Reserve missed awards 80% gross to winner, 15% sponsor, 5% treasury. Refund outcome pays 100% per entry and returns prize. Rounding is floor on aggregate protocol fee; remainder must be allocated without loss. No administrator, mutable configuration or upgrade. Request window [sale end, end+2days); callback accepted strictly before request timestamp+2days. Refunds open at deadline. Callback records result only. Settlement is permissionless, storage-only; redemption requires current ticket owner, burns claim atomically, and must revert all effects on delivery failure. Sponsor and treasury can claim independently after settlement. Never move assets between raffle clones. Quote token and Chainlink wrapper are trusted canonical dependencies; arbitrary prize contracts and ticket recipients are untrusted. Frontend discovery is advisory; transaction decisions must reread current chain state.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
