{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"_kritt_extractor_helper\":true,\"stub\":false,\"stub_explanation\":\"\",\"results\":[{\"explanation\":\"The factory accepts a caller-selected prize contract based on its own supportsInterface response, then treats ownerOf from that same untrusted contract as independent proof of escrow. A malicious ERC-721-shaped contract can have safeTransferFrom invoke the clone's onERC721Received callback with the expected factory, sponsor, and token ID without transferring an asset, and then return the clone from ownerOf. This sets the clone to Active and passes the factory's post-transfer checks. With reserveEntries set to 1, any sold raffle resolves to NftWon; settlement allocates 95% of the collected USDC to the attacker's sponsorRecipient independently of prize delivery. The malicious token can subsequently revert from transferFrom, leaving the winner unable to receive a prize or obtain a refund while the attacker withdraws the sponsor proceeds.\",\"file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol\",\"line\":129,\"malicious_input_example\":\"Deploy Evil721 where supportsInterface(0x80ac58cd) returns true, safeTransferFrom(from,to,id) calls IERC721Receiver(to).onERC721Received(msg.sender,from,id,\\\"\\\") without transferring, ownerOf(id) returns the recorded to address, and transferFrom later reverts. Call createRaffle({sponsorRecipient: attacker, prizeToken: address(Evil721), prizeTokenId: 1, reserveEntries: 1, endTime: uint64(block.timestamp + 1 days)}), then attract at least one USDC-funded entry purchase.\",\"summary\":\"A caller-controlled ERC-721 can forge prize escrow and activate an unfunded raffle\",\"trigger_flow\":[\"The attacker deploys an ERC-721-shaped contract, selects it as prizeToken, and calls RaffleFactory.createRaffle with reserveEntries equal to 1.\",\"RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams accepts the contract because its attacker-controlled supportsInterface call reports IERC721 support.\",\"The factory deploys, initializes, and registers the clone in AwaitingPrize state.\",\"RaffleFactory.createRaffle calls the malicious token's safeTransferFrom at line 128.\",\"The token directly invokes Raffle.onERC721Received with operator equal to the factory, from equal to the sponsor, and the configured token ID; Raffle.sol lines 421-430 accept these supplied values and set Active despite no genuine transfer.\",\"RaffleFactory.sol line 129 asks the same malicious token for ownerOf; it returns the clone, so the factory accepts the forged custody and emits RaffleCreated.\",\"Victims call Raffle.buyEntries and transfer canonical USDC into the clone.\",\"After the draw, reserveEntries equal to 1 guarantees NftWon; settleWinningTicket allocates 95% of the pot to sponsorProceeds, which releaseSponsorProceeds pays to the attacker.\",\"The winner's redeemWinningTicket call reaches the malicious prize token's transferFrom and reverts, leaving the NFT claim unfulfillable with no NftWon refund path.\"],\"vulnerability_type\":\"Improper validation of untrusted ERC-721 custody\",\"malicious_actor\":\"A raffle sponsor who controls the selected prize-token contract\",\"exploitable\":true}]}"}}
